<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#080711">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/dashboard.css?v=<%= File.mtime(File.join(APP_ROOT, "public", "dashboard.css")).to_i %>">
  <title>Spark</title>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container settings-page ask-page">
    <% navigation_active = "ask" %>
    <%= render_partial("navigation", binding) %>
    <header class="settings-header">
      <h1>Spark</h1>
      <span class="ask-status" data-ask-status role="status" aria-label="Spark connection status">Checking&hellip;</span>
      <div class="subtitle">Your homework helper. Ask about classes, homework, and grades, answered from what EmberGuide has saved.</div>
    </header>

    <% if !ai_enabled? %>
      <section class="card ask-setup">
        <h2>Set up Spark</h2>
        <p>Spark uses a llama.cpp server on your home network. Set <code>LLM_URL</code> (for example <code>http://192.168.1.50:8080</code>) and optionally <code>LLM_API_KEY</code> in <code>.env</code> or the Home Assistant add-on options, then restart EmberGuide.</p>
      </section>
    <% elsif !data %>
      <section class="card ask-setup">
        <p>Waiting for Canvas data. Refresh from the dashboard first.</p>
      </section>
    <% else %>
      <details class="card ask-history" data-ask-history>
        <summary data-ask-history-summary>Previous Conversations</summary>
        <p class="ask-footnote">Saved conversations are shared with everyone who can access EmberGuide and included in backups. New answers use the latest saved school data; earlier answers keep their original context.</p>
        <div class="ask-history-list" data-ask-history-list></div>
        <button type="button" class="ask-clear" data-ask-history-refresh>Refresh conversations</button>
      </details>
      <p class="ask-history-status" data-ask-history-status role="status"></p>
      <section class="card ask-card" aria-label="Conversation">
        <h2 class="ask-conversation-title" data-ask-conversation-title>New conversation</h2>
        <div class="ask-log" data-ask-log role="log" aria-label="Messages" tabindex="0" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <% suggestions = ["What should I focus on tonight?", "Summarize this week in each class.", "What should I study for upcoming tests?", "Which class needs the most attention right now?"] %>
        <div class="ask-suggestions" data-ask-suggestions>
          <% suggestions.each do |suggestion| %>
            <button type="button" class="ask-suggestion"><%= h suggestion %></button>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <div class="ask-suggestions-mobile">
          <label class="module-sr-only" for="ask-suggestion-select">Suggested questions</label>
          <select id="ask-suggestion-select" data-ask-suggestion-select>
            <option value="">Suggested questions</option>
            <% suggestions.each do |suggestion| %>
              <option value="<%= h suggestion %>"><%= h suggestion %></option>
            <% end %>
          </select>
        </div>
        <form class="ask-form" data-ask-form>
          <label class="module-sr-only" for="ask-input">Your question</label>
          <textarea id="ask-input" name="question" rows="2" maxlength="<%= AI_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS %>" placeholder="Ask Spark about homework, tests, or grades&hellip;" required></textarea>
          <div class="ask-web">
            <label class="ask-web-toggle">
              <input type="checkbox" data-ask-web-toggle>
              Search the web
            </label>
            <details class="ask-web-details">
              <summary>How web search works</summary>
              <p>Spark first identifies the study material locally, then rewrites your question as a public study topic or vocabulary search. Known student and teacher names and configured passwords or API keys are automatically removed before the search request is sent to an external web-search service for sources. Your saved grades, full class notes, and chat history are not attached. Fractions, percentages, dates, and other study terms are allowed. These steps cannot guarantee anonymity, especially for names Spark doesn't know. Leave web search off for sensitive questions. No additional API key is needed; free limits apply.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button type="button" class="ask-clear" data-ask-clear>New conversation</button>
            <button type="submit" class="ask-send">Ask</button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <p class="ask-footnote">Spark runs on a local AI model and can be wrong. Check Canvas or ask the teacher for anything important.</p>
      </section>

      <details class="card ask-context">
        <summary>What Spark can see (about <%= format_number((ai_context.length / 4.0).round(-2)) %> tokens)</summary>
        <pre><%= h ai_context %></pre>
      </details>
    <% end %>
  </main>
  <script src="/ask.js?v=<%= File.mtime(File.join(APP_ROOT, "public", "ask.js")).to_i %>" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
